1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:02,769
Quadratics are a core
part of Advanced Math,

2
00:00:02,789 --> 00:00:07,376
which is about thirty-five
percent of the SAT math section.

3
00:00:07,396 --> 00:00:11,325
And most quadratic questions
come down to one idea.

4
00:00:11,361 --> 00:00:14,020
The same parabola can be
written three different ways,

5
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:16,468
and each way shows you
something different.

6
00:00:16,555 --> 00:00:19,427
Students lose points by
fighting with the wrong form,

7
00:00:19,447 --> 00:00:21,499
or by answering with the wrong number.

8
00:00:21,519 --> 00:00:23,519
The time instead of the height.

9
00:00:23,661 --> 00:00:27,891
The x coordinate of the vertex when
the question asked for the maximum.

10
00:00:27,911 --> 00:00:31,875
In this video: the three forms
and what each one reveals,

11
00:00:31,911 --> 00:00:35,284
factoring, the quadratic
formula, the discriminant,

12
00:00:35,304 --> 00:00:40,339
max and min word problems, and the
sum and product of the solutions.

13
00:00:40,590 --> 00:00:44,018
Six practice questions, from easy to hard.

14
00:00:44,096 --> 00:00:46,539
Here's one parabola, written three ways.

15
00:00:46,559 --> 00:00:52,132
Standard form: y equals x
squared minus six x plus eight.

16
00:00:52,739 --> 00:00:57,362
Factored form: y equals x
minus two, times x minus four.

17
00:00:57,382 --> 00:01:00,933
Vertex form: y equals
x minus three, squared,

18
00:01:00,953 --> 00:01:01,933
minus one.

19
00:01:01,953 --> 00:01:03,739
All three make the same graph.

20
00:01:03,803 --> 00:01:05,604
Standard form shows the y intercept.

21
00:01:05,624 --> 00:01:09,497
It's the constant at the end, so this
parabola crosses the y axis at eight.

22
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:11,997
The leading coefficient
shows the direction.

23
00:01:12,017 --> 00:01:13,247
Positive opens up.

24
00:01:13,267 --> 00:01:14,980
Negative opens down.

25
00:01:15,021 --> 00:01:17,643
Factored form shows the x intercepts,

26
00:01:17,663 --> 00:01:21,199
also called the zeros,
roots, or solutions.

27
00:01:21,271 --> 00:01:23,949
Set each factor equal to zero.

28
00:01:24,091 --> 00:01:29,215
x minus two gives two, and
x minus four gives four.

29
00:01:29,235 --> 00:01:30,413
Watch the sign.

30
00:01:30,592 --> 00:01:34,592
The factor says minus two,
but the root is positive two.

31
00:01:34,614 --> 00:01:36,665
Vertex form shows the vertex.

32
00:01:36,685 --> 00:01:40,416
x minus three, squared, minus
one puts the vertex at three,

33
00:01:40,436 --> 00:01:41,451
negative one.

34
00:01:41,471 --> 00:01:45,201
The x part flips sign again, but
the constant at the end doesn't.

35
00:01:45,221 --> 00:01:49,257
Since this parabola opens up,
negative one is its minimum value.

36
00:01:49,282 --> 00:01:51,104
Two more facts connect the forms.

37
00:01:51,211 --> 00:01:56,461
From standard form, the x coordinate
of the vertex is negative b over two a.

38
00:01:56,531 --> 00:01:59,226
Here, that's six over two, which is three.

39
00:01:59,246 --> 00:02:03,191
And the vertex always sits exactly
halfway between the two roots.

40
00:02:03,211 --> 00:02:05,461
Halfway between two and four is three.

41
00:02:05,528 --> 00:02:09,350
The SAT tests quadratics
in a few predictable ways.

42
00:02:09,385 --> 00:02:10,778
Solve the equation.

43
00:02:10,814 --> 00:02:12,686
Pick the form that shows a feature.

44
00:02:12,706 --> 00:02:14,865
Decide how many solutions there are.

45
00:02:14,885 --> 00:02:18,007
Find a maximum or minimum
in a word problem.

46
00:02:18,027 --> 00:02:21,180
And use the sum or
product of the solutions.

47
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:25,236
The key on every one: before
you calculate anything,

48
00:02:25,271 --> 00:02:29,057
ask which form, or which formula,
gives you the answer for free.

49
00:02:29,129 --> 00:02:30,002
Question one.

50
00:02:30,022 --> 00:02:34,859
What are the solutions to the equation
x squared minus two x minus fifteen

51
00:02:34,879 --> 00:02:35,914
equals zero?

52
00:02:35,936 --> 00:02:37,578
Pause and try it.

53
00:02:40,809 --> 00:02:45,325
To factor, find two numbers that
multiply to negative fifteen and add to

54
00:02:45,345 --> 00:02:46,631
negative two.

55
00:02:46,702 --> 00:02:48,988
Negative five and three work.

56
00:02:49,023 --> 00:02:51,952
Negative five times three
is negative fifteen,

57
00:02:51,988 --> 00:02:55,059
and negative five plus
three is negative two.

58
00:02:55,110 --> 00:02:57,696
So the equation becomes x minus five,

59
00:02:57,716 --> 00:03:00,947
times x plus three, equals zero.

60
00:03:00,967 --> 00:03:02,660
Set each factor to zero.

61
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:06,160
x equals five, or x equals negative three.

62
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:07,788
The answer is B.

63
00:03:07,817 --> 00:03:09,546
A is the sign trap.

64
00:03:09,566 --> 00:03:13,047
Negative five and three are
the numbers inside the factors,

65
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,424
not the solutions.

66
00:03:14,531 --> 00:03:16,745
If you're ever unsure, plug one back in.

67
00:03:16,853 --> 00:03:20,083
Negative five gives twenty-five
plus ten minus fifteen,

68
00:03:20,103 --> 00:03:22,017
which is twenty, not zero.

69
00:03:22,037 --> 00:03:23,251
Question two.

70
00:03:23,429 --> 00:03:29,481
The function f is defined by f of x
equals x squared plus four x minus

71
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:30,501
twenty-one.

72
00:03:30,679 --> 00:03:34,981
Which of the following equivalent forms
of f of x displays the minimum value of

73
00:03:35,001 --> 00:03:37,429
f as a constant or coefficient?

74
00:03:37,506 --> 00:03:39,148
Pause and try it.

75
00:03:42,379 --> 00:03:45,538
Minimum value means the y
coordinate of the vertex.

76
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:48,252
The form that shows the
vertex is vertex form:

77
00:03:48,272 --> 00:03:51,109
something squared, plus
or minus a constant,

78
00:03:51,129 --> 00:03:52,573
with nothing else attached.

79
00:03:52,593 --> 00:03:53,430
That's C.

80
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:56,108
x plus two, squared, minus twenty-five.

81
00:03:56,128 --> 00:03:59,129
The minimum value is negative twenty-five.

82
00:03:59,245 --> 00:04:01,795
A is factored form, so it shows the zeros,

83
00:04:01,815 --> 00:04:03,638
three and negative seven.

84
00:04:04,031 --> 00:04:06,923
B shows the y intercept,
negative twenty-one.

85
00:04:07,173 --> 00:04:08,546
And D is the trap.

86
00:04:08,566 --> 00:04:15,118
It has a squared term, but the extra ten
times the quantity x minus three means

87
00:04:15,138 --> 00:04:16,813
it isn't vertex form.

88
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:21,706
To double check in Desmos, graph y
equals x squared plus four x minus

89
00:04:21,726 --> 00:04:25,242
twenty-one, zoom out, and
click the bottom of the curve.

90
00:04:25,262 --> 00:04:27,904
It shows negative two,
negative twenty-five.

91
00:04:28,038 --> 00:04:30,411
When a quadratic won't factor nicely,

92
00:04:30,431 --> 00:04:32,232
use the quadratic formula.

93
00:04:32,252 --> 00:04:39,339
x equals negative b, plus or minus the
square root of b squared minus four a c,

94
00:04:39,359 --> 00:04:41,052
all over two a.

95
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:41,873
Question three.

96
00:04:41,893 --> 00:04:47,179
What are the solutions to two x squared
minus six x plus three equals zero?

97
00:04:47,215 --> 00:04:48,858
Pause and try it.

98
00:04:53,088 --> 00:04:58,247
Here a is two, b is negative
six, and c is three.

99
00:04:58,267 --> 00:05:00,231
Start with the part under the square root.

100
00:05:00,445 --> 00:05:04,426
b squared minus four a c is
thirty-six minus twenty-four,

101
00:05:04,446 --> 00:05:05,553
which is twelve.

102
00:05:05,670 --> 00:05:09,650
So x equals six, plus or minus
the square root of twelve,

103
00:05:09,670 --> 00:05:10,650
all over four.

104
00:05:10,670 --> 00:05:13,543
The square root of
twelve is two root three.

105
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:18,079
Divide every term by two, and you
get three plus or minus root three,

106
00:05:18,099 --> 00:05:19,293
all over two.

107
00:05:19,313 --> 00:05:20,799
The answer is B.

108
00:05:20,819 --> 00:05:25,406
C is what you get if you
divide by two instead of two a.

109
00:05:25,426 --> 00:05:28,727
D comes from adding four a
c instead of subtracting it.

110
00:05:28,747 --> 00:05:31,726
And A uses b instead of negative b.

111
00:05:31,746 --> 00:05:34,569
Here, negative b is positive six.

112
00:05:34,593 --> 00:05:35,930
Desmos check.

113
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:39,680
Graph y equals two x squared
minus six x plus three,

114
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:41,466
and click the x intercepts.

115
00:05:41,486 --> 00:05:46,894
You get about zero point six three
four and two point three six six.

116
00:05:46,914 --> 00:05:50,466
Then type three plus
root three, all over two,

117
00:05:50,486 --> 00:05:52,057
on its own line.

118
00:05:52,521 --> 00:05:55,394
Desmos shows two point three six six.

119
00:05:55,414 --> 00:05:56,479
It matches.

120
00:05:56,499 --> 00:05:59,978
The part under the square
root, b squared minus four a c,

121
00:05:59,998 --> 00:06:01,300
is called the discriminant.

122
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:04,907
It tells you how many real
solutions there are without solving.

123
00:06:04,927 --> 00:06:06,693
Positive means two.

124
00:06:06,713 --> 00:06:08,729
Zero means exactly one.

125
00:06:08,749 --> 00:06:10,446
Negative means none.

126
00:06:10,466 --> 00:06:14,553
On a graph, that's how many times
the parabola meets the x axis.

127
00:06:14,573 --> 00:06:17,802
It crosses twice, touches
once at the vertex,

128
00:06:17,822 --> 00:06:19,235
or never reaches it.

129
00:06:19,255 --> 00:06:20,398
Question four.

130
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:24,842
In the equation nine x squared
minus twelve x plus c equals zero,

131
00:06:24,862 --> 00:06:26,148
c is a constant.

132
00:06:26,326 --> 00:06:29,592
If the equation has
exactly one real solution,

133
00:06:29,612 --> 00:06:31,434
what is the value of c?

134
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:33,159
Pause and try it.

135
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:40,212
Exactly one solution means
the discriminant equals zero.

136
00:06:40,390 --> 00:06:42,549
b squared is negative twelve squared,

137
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:43,869
which is one hundred forty-four.

138
00:06:43,889 --> 00:06:49,477
Four a c is four times nine
times c, or thirty-six c.

139
00:06:49,497 --> 00:06:53,727
So one hundred forty-four
minus thirty-six c equals zero,

140
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:55,447
and c equals four.

141
00:06:55,467 --> 00:06:56,304
Check it.

142
00:06:56,324 --> 00:07:00,768
Nine x squared minus twelve x
plus four is three x minus two,

143
00:07:00,788 --> 00:07:03,823
squared, a perfect
square with one solution.

144
00:07:04,038 --> 00:07:09,375
In Desmos, graph y equals nine
x squared minus twelve x plus c,

145
00:07:09,395 --> 00:07:14,277
add a slider for c, and drag until
the parabola just touches the x axis.

146
00:07:14,297 --> 00:07:16,617
That happens at c equals four.

147
00:07:16,665 --> 00:07:18,109
Question five.

148
00:07:18,129 --> 00:07:21,787
A company models its daily
profit P, in dollars,

149
00:07:21,807 --> 00:07:26,716
from selling a product at a price of p
dollars with the function P of p equals

150
00:07:26,736 --> 00:07:30,179
negative five p squared,
plus two hundred p,

151
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:32,055
minus one thousand two hundred.

152
00:07:32,075 --> 00:07:35,412
According to the model, what
is the maximum daily profit,

153
00:07:35,432 --> 00:07:36,526
in dollars?

154
00:07:36,546 --> 00:07:38,189
Pause and try it.

155
00:07:42,419 --> 00:07:46,542
The leading coefficient is negative,
so the parabola opens down,

156
00:07:46,562 --> 00:07:48,828
and the vertex is the maximum.

157
00:07:48,848 --> 00:07:53,184
The p coordinate of the vertex
is negative b over two a.

158
00:07:53,204 --> 00:07:55,757
That's negative two
hundred over negative ten,

159
00:07:55,777 --> 00:07:56,899
which is twenty.

160
00:07:56,919 --> 00:07:59,101
Twenty dollars is the best price.

161
00:07:59,121 --> 00:08:00,550
But they asked for the profit.

162
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,085
Plug in twenty.

163
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:06,207
Negative five times four hundred
is negative two thousand.

164
00:08:06,227 --> 00:08:09,477
Two hundred times twenty is four thousand.

165
00:08:09,513 --> 00:08:11,708
Negative two thousand, plus four thousand,

166
00:08:11,728 --> 00:08:14,672
minus one thousand two
hundred, is eight hundred.

167
00:08:14,692 --> 00:08:16,264
The answer is B.

168
00:08:16,310 --> 00:08:17,361
Twenty is the trap.

169
00:08:17,381 --> 00:08:19,452
It's the price, not the profit.

170
00:08:19,524 --> 00:08:22,540
Two thousand eight hundred
drops the squared term.

171
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:25,214
Four thousand eight hundred
gets its sign wrong.

172
00:08:25,234 --> 00:08:28,270
In Desmos, type it with x instead of p,

173
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:30,679
zoom out, and click the top of the curve.

174
00:08:30,699 --> 00:08:33,270
Desmos shows twenty, eight hundred.

175
00:08:33,483 --> 00:08:35,139
The second number is the profit.

176
00:08:35,159 --> 00:08:36,032
Last concept.

177
00:08:36,052 --> 00:08:39,996
For any quadratic, a x
squared plus b x plus c,

178
00:08:40,016 --> 00:08:42,245
the solutions add up to negative b over a,

179
00:08:42,265 --> 00:08:44,960
and they multiply to c over a.

180
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:47,766
You don't have to find
the solutions to use this.

181
00:08:47,829 --> 00:08:48,737
Quick example.

182
00:08:48,757 --> 00:08:52,987
x squared minus seven x plus
ten has solutions two and five.

183
00:08:53,007 --> 00:08:55,522
They add to seven, which
is negative b over a.

184
00:08:55,542 --> 00:08:59,164
And they multiply to
ten, which is c over a.

185
00:08:59,184 --> 00:09:01,220
Question six, the hardest one.

186
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:06,377
The solutions to the equation three x
squared plus b x plus c equals zero,

187
00:09:06,397 --> 00:09:10,898
where b and c are constants, are
four and negative two thirds.

188
00:09:10,970 --> 00:09:13,541
What is the value of b plus c?

189
00:09:13,565 --> 00:09:14,581
Pause and try it.

190
00:09:14,601 --> 00:09:16,101
Take a little longer on this one.

191
00:09:20,337 --> 00:09:21,444
Start with the sum.

192
00:09:21,552 --> 00:09:23,960
Four plus negative two
thirds is ten thirds.

193
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:27,853
The sum is negative b
over a, and a is three.

194
00:09:27,873 --> 00:09:30,638
So negative b over
three equals ten thirds,

195
00:09:30,658 --> 00:09:32,659
and b equals negative ten.

196
00:09:32,686 --> 00:09:33,487
Now the product.

197
00:09:33,507 --> 00:09:37,436
Four times negative two thirds
is negative eight thirds.

198
00:09:37,507 --> 00:09:42,309
The product is c over a, so c over
three equals negative eight thirds,

199
00:09:42,329 --> 00:09:44,523
and c equals negative eight.

200
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:48,594
So b plus c is negative
ten plus negative eight,

201
00:09:48,614 --> 00:09:50,363
which is negative eighteen.

202
00:09:50,383 --> 00:09:52,577
You can confirm it with factored form.

203
00:09:52,597 --> 00:09:56,041
A solution of four means
a factor of x minus four.

204
00:09:56,061 --> 00:10:01,240
A solution of negative two thirds
means a factor of three x plus two.

205
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:06,490
Multiply them, and you get three
x squared minus ten x minus eight.

206
00:10:06,633 --> 00:10:08,419
Same b, same c.

207
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:10,128
The trap is forgetting the a.

208
00:10:10,378 --> 00:10:15,144
If you treat the sum as just
negative b and the product as just c,

209
00:10:15,164 --> 00:10:18,450
you get fractions for b and
c, and the wrong answer.

210
00:10:18,525 --> 00:10:20,219
Here's the test-day checklist.

211
00:10:20,239 --> 00:10:23,541
First, read exactly what
they want: the solutions,

212
00:10:23,561 --> 00:10:26,218
the vertex, a maximum or minimum value,

213
00:10:26,238 --> 00:10:29,204
the number of solutions,
or a sum or product.

214
00:10:29,347 --> 00:10:31,488
Then reach for the matching tool.

215
00:10:31,508 --> 00:10:37,258
Solutions: factor if it's quick,
otherwise use the formula or Desmos.

216
00:10:37,436 --> 00:10:41,864
Vertex, max, or min:
negative b over two a,

217
00:10:42,079 --> 00:10:45,258
vertex form, or click the
top or bottom of the graph.

218
00:10:46,008 --> 00:10:48,793
Number of solutions: the discriminant.

219
00:10:49,115 --> 00:10:54,579
Sum or product: negative
b over a, and c over a.

220
00:10:54,601 --> 00:10:57,530
And before you lock in an
answer, reread the question.

221
00:10:58,315 --> 00:11:00,458
A vertex has two numbers.

222
00:11:00,565 --> 00:11:02,851
Make sure you're giving
the one they asked for.

223
00:11:02,885 --> 00:11:03,615
Recap.

224
00:11:03,635 --> 00:11:06,455
Standard form shows the y intercept.

225
00:11:06,528 --> 00:11:09,686
Factored form shows the
roots, with the signs flipped.

226
00:11:09,706 --> 00:11:13,114
Vertex form shows the
vertex, and the max or min.

227
00:11:13,134 --> 00:11:15,186
The discriminant counts solutions.

228
00:11:15,206 --> 00:11:20,691
And the solutions add to negative
b over a and multiply to c over a.

229
00:11:20,711 --> 00:11:25,226
Every question in this video was written
for this video in the style of the real

230
00:11:25,246 --> 00:11:26,048
test.

231
00:11:26,068 --> 00:11:30,262
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

232
00:11:30,282 --> 00:11:32,911
domain, skill, and difficulty.

233
00:11:32,931 --> 00:11:34,681
If this helped, subscribe.

234
00:11:34,895 --> 00:11:37,590
Next up is linear functions
and word problems,

235
00:11:37,610 --> 00:11:41,074
including how to read what
the slope actually means.
